  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="6b16ca2b-c34b-57e3-875a-e622d83b3f13" activityNameId="930473af-9019-5376-a0db-1f853733d0c8" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Agricultural machinery, tillage, production</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Agricultural machinery, tillage, production
Representatives of this class are for example: plough, harrow or roller. Calculations are made with a mean machinery of 800 kg, 800 hours useful life and 0.72 repair factor. For exact results, module should only be used if lifetime and repair factor of the balanced machinery are within a narrow range of the values the module is based on. The functional unit is 1kg machinery during its lifetime.;
UUID: cef8d695-fdaf-36ef-83ca-66188d23fdfc
The inventory takes into account the use of resources and the amount of emissions during the production, the maintenance and repair and the disposal of agricultural tillage machinery. Not taken into account were the impacts caused by fuel consumption during operation-time of the trailing machinery. No data was available about buildings needed for manufacture and maintenance of the machinery. The routes needed for transport from manufacturer place to the farm and from here to disposal place of the waste, are balanced in the utilised transport modules.
Location: The inventories apply to the production in Western Europe and transportation to Switzerland.
Technology: Values are based and adapted on a different technology (lorries-manufacture).
Time period: Considered references range from start- to end-date
Production volume: na
Sampling: Values given in the reference originate mainly from studies about lorry production in Europe as examined and adapted by Zimmermann (2002) and experts estimations. 
Extrapolations: Data are extrapolated, examined and adapted from lorry production in Europe.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_cef8d695-fdaf-36ef-83ca-66188d23fdfc.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="fdab769f-4bdb-5024-8349-c1745bbb2597" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
